  "notes": "French system classes. The school year runs from February to December. Primary schooling is run by New Caledonia (DENC) with its own programmes, grouped in cycle 2 (CP, CE1) and cycle 3 (CE2, CM1, CM2); collège and lycée are overseen by the vice-rectorat. The brevet closes 3e and the baccalauréat closes Terminale; vocational lycée pupils say Seconde pro, Première pro and Terminale pro."
